LoveCloud third-party notices
============================

The Apache-2.0 license in LICENSE covers LoveCloud's original code and project
materials only. It does not relicense dependencies, operating-system packages,
fonts or any material expressly marked with a different license.

Fonts (unmodified, local files)
------------------------------
Caveat: Copyright 2014 The Caveat Project Authors.
Golos Text: see the exact copyright statement in licenses/GolosText-OFL.txt.
Rubik: see the exact copyright statement in licenses/Rubik-OFL.txt.
All three use SIL Open Font License 1.1. Copies accompany this distribution and
frontend/public/fonts/. The preview carries its own copies. The README banner
contains outlined forms from Caveat and Golos Text, not a redistributed font.

JavaScript
----------
Next.js (MIT), React / React DOM (MIT), SWR (MIT), Microsoft SignalR (MIT),
qrcode (MIT) and their runtime dependencies retain their original notices.
Browser-bundled dependencies are covered by a separate notices-only production
graph; server standalone tracing alone is not a client license inventory.
SignalR npm omits its own MIT file; licenses/SignalR-LICENSE.txt preserves the
official release text, alongside its shipped es6-promise third-party notices.
The exact runtime packages are collected from the shipped image, rather than
assuming every optional entry in package-lock.json is installed.

Next.js can bring sharp (Apache-2.0) and platform-specific @img packages into a
standalone image. Their mere presence in package-lock.json does not mean they
ship. LoveCloud does not use next/image; the unused optimizer is disabled and
sharp/@img are excluded before the final runtime image COPY. The release gate
inspects both the final filesystem and image layers to confirm this exclusion.

Build-only @img/sharp-libvips 1.3.4 declares LGPL-3.0-or-later (libvips8.18.7 and
its own third-party components). This optional native stack is not part of the
runtime distribution. Do not reintroduce it without its full corresponding
sources, build/relinking material and applicable notices. See
licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt, LGPL-3.0.txt, GPL-3.0.txt and docs/LICENSING_AUDIT.md.

.NET
----
ASP.NET Core, .NET runtime, Entity Framework Core and Microsoft libraries: MIT,
with embedded third-party notices. Npgsql and its EF Core provider: PostgreSQL
License; exact-version full Npgsql notices/provenance are preserved in
licenses/Npgsql-LICENSE.txt, Npgsql-EFCore-LICENSE.txt and nuget-license-index.json.
SkiaSharp: MIT, Xamarin / Microsoft copyrights preserved in
licenses/SkiaSharp-LICENSE.txt. Native libSkiaSharp also incorporates Skia and
other libraries under their own licenses. The NuGet package's aggregated
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES is collected into the release licensing bundle.

Container operating systems and infrastructure
----------------------------------------------
Node.js, Alpine Linux / musl / BusyBox / OpenSSL, .NET's Linux distribution,
nginx, PostgreSQL, and optional Caddy / Tailscale remain separately licensed.
SBOMs describe the actual release image digests. Image-bundled license texts and
package/source metadata are retained in the collected licensing bundle.
BusyBox and alpine-baselayout in the actual Alpine runtime are GPL-2.0-only;
licenses/GPL-2.0.txt contains the full GNU text, and the release source bundle
includes their exact APKBUILD recipes and checksum-verified sources.
Sources for the exact Alpine packages are available through the matching
Alpine package repository; Debian/Ubuntu sources through their corresponding
source package repositories. Consult the SBOM and recorded image provenance.

Images, illustrations and preview
--------------------------------
LoveCloud vector illustrations and documentation screenshots are project
materials, subject to the original-material ownership record in
docs/LICENSING_AUDIT.md. Screenshots use a fictional couple and synthetic data.
The public interactive preview uses local vector illustrations and local fonts.
It makes no request to Unsplash, Google Fonts, a LoveCloud API or analytics.
Historical prototype screenshots with uncertain stock-photo attribution were
removed from this release source tree. The app theme cards use synthetic actual-
app screenshots. Their provenance and exclusion are recorded in the audit.

Release artifacts
-----------------
The exact-image SBOMs and collected licenses/source bundle accompany releases.
For v0.1.0, full native/distribution source, recipes and notices are provided at:
https://github.com/m0rp3x/LoveCloud/releases/download/v0.1.0/lovecloud-v0.1.0-third-party-licenses.tar.gz
This includes immutable SkiaSharp/Skia build source and zlib/mozzconf source for
historical MPL-1.1 tri-licensed components named in the upstream native notices.
See licenses/MPL-1.1.txt; no LoveCloud modifications to those components are made.
Run scripts/release/collect-licenses.py against the final API/frontend digests
to reproduce the license inventory. An inventory is evidence of the shipped
files, not a substitute for the individual licenses and notices themselves.
